rivacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":656,"digest":"sha256:94b974c9c52bea37393a186f63cd5c20d72b2dd3ccf379949493587edb022192","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-18T17:26:53Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T17:26:53Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m1310-v0.13.10/m13stage10-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m1310-v0.13.10","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m1310-v0.13.10","body":"# Engacer OS M13.10 / 0.13.10 - Polished dialogs and app frames\n\nExact native qualification passes M13-STAGE10-VM-v1. This is a scoped testing release; website publication is a separate closure gate. Stability investigation and duration/reset-chain qualification remain exclusively M13.13 after M13.10-M13.12.\n\nUse the matching [installation guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/e83df9e814547a54bc4515e28a47592f37a1b342/docs/handbook/install-m1310.md), [common dialogs](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/e83df9e814547a54bc4515e28a47592f37a1b342/docs/handbook/dialogs-m1310.md), [Settings](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/e83df9e814547a54bc4515e28a47592f37a1b342/docs/handbook/settings-m1310.md) and [standard apps](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/e83df9e814547a54bc4515e28a47592f37a1b342/docs/handbook/apps-m1310.md).\n\n## Exact media\n\n- Build: `9f0aa4da90a258c8027b557544666fdf`.\n- ISO SHA256: `97477f70da45047f2344baa9bcfd9db41ad10cc0f2dee7890910b3d1ffa8f2a7`.\n- VMware ZIP SHA256: `6925605caebf1c68d361d5112f1d2c2c70dbb3824b75edf22269364bf221900c`.\n\nThe exact VMware starter includes a blank growable 20-GiB SATA disk, two CPUs, 128 MiB RAM, UEFI and Secure Boot off. Extract the full ZIP and open EngacerOS.vmx. No preinstalled desktop, disabled shipped device or forced boot order substitutes for the real installation and independent startups.\n\n## What changes\n\nSettings uses a Search results heading, a readable Clear search button and result-only content without unrelated appearance Apply controls. A pending preview remains explicitly described. Appearance-write refusal retains a concise recovery message within the existing 96-byte notice, so Cancel preview stays visible without growing application state.\n\nOpen/Save/folder dialogs use the same vector Back/Forward/Up icons as Files. Shared file dialogs gain a semantic header icon and clear High-contrast boundary. Existing history, disabled choices, ordinary selection, long paths, explicit replacement and dirty-document ownership remain authoritative.\n\nPointer context refreshes after keyboard-driven scene changes as well as pointer movement. Supported preview/filename fields show the text cursor. This adds no retained desktop state, bitmap, framebuffer, timer or idle worker. The included offline guide explains pointer feedback.\n\n## Qualification matrix and limits\n\nShared controls, Settings and secondary dialogs cover five named display profiles and three themes. Standard-app frames cover all nineteen window kinds in Light at ordinary, compact, 1024, 150% and physical 4K, plus all nineteen in Dark/High contrast at ordinary size. Every app control must remain inside its real owner window and closing must return managed pages. This is an explicit matrix, not a claimed Cartesian product or human novice study.\n\nActual install/startup, real file-byte comparisons, a controlled injected write refusal, independent optional-app management and the exact enabled-device starter pass on these exact bytes. [Native acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/e83df9e814547a54bc4515e28a47592f37a1b342/evidence/M13/10/acceptance-results.json) records 133 native checks and 3 exact VMware checks. All 133 declared app frames pass; [resource evidence](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/e83df9e814547a54bc4515e28a47592f37a1b342/evidence/M13/10/resources.json) records unchanged fixed desktop state (557,404 bytes), unchanged installer state and zero completed-task retention.\n\nThe initial 04a86775 candidate is withdrawn because its appearance failure text exceeded the notice buffer. Its observations and intentionally interrupted remaining tasks are retained as diagnostics. The corrected candidate passes fresh functional qualification. These controlled failure tasks and ordinary independent starts do not qualify stability; all natural-freeze, duration and reset-chain work remains M13.13.\n\nThis stage does not requalify physical refresh/FPS, universal hardware, vendor GPU 3D or general Windows compatibility. Historical M13.9 processing measurements do not certify these new media. Final whole-product controller/application integration remains M13.12.\n\n## Licensing\n\nOriginal project contributions retain MIT licensing. Included third-party components keep their notices and corresponding license/source assets. The matching release must contain twenty complete assets and exact checksums.\n"}